{:edb/db-before-t 2136 :edb/db-after-t 2137 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535449 50 #inst "2026-10-09T00:19:28.414Z" 13194139535449 true] [17592186078517 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349678 13194139535449 true] [17592186078517 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349682 13194139535449 true] [17592186078518 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349685 13194139535449 true] [17592186078946 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065207/assets/83b23d8138091a931d14854b197752d25d8149ee8914a70b8db73b6c2369c888.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535449 true] [17592186078946 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040192/assets/83b23d8138091a931d14854b197752d25d8149ee8914a70b8db73b6c2369c888.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535449 false] [17592186293780 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065207/assets/d36f2859865da58d226a738d8338f726df950db75b7421b604bb692c9049d54a.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535449 true] [17592186293780 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061763/assets/d36f2859865da58d226a738d8338f726df950db75b7421b604bb692c9049d54a.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535449 false] [17592186349678 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349679 13194139535449 true] [17592186349678 1089 "q-338331" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349678 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535449 true] [17592186349678 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065207/assets/06ace831b877406e48fe8f1ab38a7244e7ade878d7c77b99d8230f40ad307207.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of four line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535449 true] [17592186349678 1113 #uuid "3010a5d1-7b47-53cc-a84b-d481e0b19c2e" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349678 1145 "The graph consists of four parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-6,-3],$ the line segment for $x\\in (-3,0],$ the line segment for $x\\in (0,2],$ and the line segment for $x\\in (2,5].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-6}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{4}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-6,-3].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}3(3) \\\\  & =4.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-3,0].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =bh \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (0,2].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4+2)(2) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (2,5].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}3(6) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}+{A}_{4} \\\\  & =4.5+3+6+9 \\\\  & =22.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349680 13194139535449 true] [17592186349679 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349681 13194139535449 true] [17592186349679 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535449 true] [17592186349679 1041 "field-1" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349679 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349681 13194139535449 true] [17592186349679 1110 #uuid "d125695a-c155-5239-9b5f-5b6e05520a60" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349680 1034 "45" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349680 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535449 true] [17592186349680 1111 #uuid "8a028ffc-68fc-56aa-9e1f-12f2e817955e" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349681 1034 "\\frac{45}{2}" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349681 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535449 true] [17592186349681 1111 #uuid "611f6b0e-9f94-5fa2-9203-2bb6b690e6da" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349682 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349683 13194139535449 true] [17592186349682 1089 "q-338336" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349682 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535449 true] [17592186349682 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065207/assets/19b94b149f752dc284f2cc002d786bc002621333a8eaadf2396e131640046c89.png)\n\nThe graph $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of two line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535449 true] [17592186349682 1113 #uuid "a967fa2f-cf50-596f-b417-99d097139ba9" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349682 1145 "We divide the interval of integration into $3$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-5,0],$ the line segment for $x\\in (0,3],$ and the line segment for $x\\in [3,5].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-5}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-5,0].$   The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+4)(5) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (0,3].$    The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3+0)(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$   The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+2)(2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{3}=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}-{A}_{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{2}+\\frac{9}{2}-2 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349683 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349684 13194139535449 true] [17592186349683 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535449 true] [17592186349683 1041 "field-1" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349683 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349684 13194139535449 true] [17592186349683 1110 #uuid "47bd312d-0b86-53fa-8d24-e7da5c89a0ee" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349684 1034 "15" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349684 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535449 true] [17592186349684 1111 #uuid "68a8cc72-ed57-55c6-b912-bef9bcbc34b2" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349685 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349686 13194139535449 true] [17592186349685 1089 "q-339266" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349685 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535449 true] [17592186349685 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14065207/assets/f418496b3460fddc13ea2beb4c099e97ed4d2fa1d89e04c01862d142e4d4177f.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139535449 true] [17592186349685 1113 #uuid "98021bae-338d-5362-9995-8e98cc8d72d8" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349685 1145 "The graph consists of $3$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-6,-3),$ the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in (-3,3),$ and the line segment for $x\\in (3,6].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-6}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-6,-3).$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4+1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-3,3).$ The corresponding region is a combination of a semi-circle of radius $3$ and a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =bh+\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =6(1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\pi (3)^{2} \\\\  & =6+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (3,6].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}+6+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}+\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =18+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349686 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349687 13194139535449 true] [17592186349686 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535449 true] [17592186349686 1041 "field-1" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349686 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349687 13194139535449 true] [17592186349686 1110 #uuid "ddd8f320-8e7b-54fd-956a-5b186a08dbb7" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349687 1034 "18+\\frac{9\\pi}{2}" 13194139535449 true] [17592186349687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535449 true] [17592186349687 1111 #uuid "06c9540c-cff1-5224-9d33-42957263b6dd" 13194139535449 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-338331" 17592186349678 "q-338331/field-1" 17592186349679 "q-338331/field-1/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" 17592186349680 "q-338331/field-1/f70b243a79f7565451b51a30aa09b35a857f215546db282029bd48de7b7b646d" 17592186349681 "q-338336" 17592186349682 "q-338336/field-1" 17592186349683 "q-338336/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" 17592186349684 "q-339266" 17592186349685 "q-339266/field-1" 17592186349686 "q-339266/field-1/6e411f361af12d52715754efc925187f62c23d9da9e98606a5dc379100660487" 17592186349687} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
